---
// SeoContent Component
// Comprehensive educational content, typing tutorials, Loksewa guides, and keyword-rich resources
---

<section class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">

    <!-- Section 1: Overview -->
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4 tracking-tight">
        Master Nepali Typing: English, Unicode Traditional, Romanized & Preeti ASCII
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Welcome to the most comprehensive and modern <strong>Nepali Typing Test platform</strong>. Whether you are practicing for the <strong>Loksewa Aayog (Public Service Commission) Computer Skill Test</strong>, banking exams (Nepal Rastra Bank, Rastriya Banijya Bank), Nepal Police, judicial services, or simply aiming to master daily Devanagari communication, this interactive workbench delivers unmatched accuracy and speed benchmarking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our platform supports all four major keyboard layouts used across Nepal: <strong>English QWERTY</strong>, <strong>Nepali Unicode (Traditional)</strong>, <strong>Nepali Unicode (Romanized)</strong>, and the legacy <strong>Preeti ASCII</strong> typewriter standard with real-time hardware keyboard mapping and millisecond-accurate metrics.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: Comparison Grid -->
    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4">
        Quick Comparison: Preeti vs Unicode Traditional vs Romanized
      </h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-xs text-left">
          <thead class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)] font-semibold">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-2.5 pr-4">Feature</th>
              <th class="py-2.5 pr-4">Preeti (ASCII)</th>
              <th class="py-2.5 pr-4">Unicode Traditional</th>
              <th class="py-2.5">Unicode Romanized</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Character Encoding</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Legacy ASCII font glyphs</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Universal UTF-8 Devanagari</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Universal UTF-8 Devanagari</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Layout Origin</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Remington typewriter layout</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Government & MPP Standard</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Phonetic English QWERTY</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Browser / Search Friendly</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 text-red-500 font-medium">No (requires local font)</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 text-emerald-500 font-medium">Yes (100% SEO searchable)</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 text-emerald-500 font-medium">Yes (100% SEO searchable)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Exam Relevance</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Loksewa & Private Presses</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Loksewa Aayog Standard</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Official Communications</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">How to Type 'क'</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-mono">Press 's'</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-mono">Press 's'</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 font-mono">Press 'k'</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: Loksewa Aayog Standards -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-950 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-3">
          🇳🇵
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">
          Loksewa Aayog Typing Test Syllabus
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs mb-3">
          Loksewa Aayog conducts computer practical tests (कम्प्युटर सीप परीक्षण) for Kharidar, Nayab Subba, and Section Officer positions:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-xs space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          <li><strong>Test Duration:</strong> 5 Minutes (300 Seconds).</li>
          <li><strong>Nepali Pass Benchmark:</strong> Minimum 20 Net WPM with at least 85% accuracy.</li>
          <li><strong>English Pass Benchmark:</strong> Minimum 25 Net WPM.</li>
          <li><strong>Error Penalty:</strong> Each incorrect word or skipped character reduces your overall net score.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-950 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-3">
          📊
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">
          How WPM & CPM Are Calculated
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs mb-3">
          We adhere to international standardized typing speed formulas:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] p-3 rounded-xl font-mono text-[11px] space-y-1 text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          <div>Raw WPM = (Total Keystrokes / 5) / Minutes</div>
          <div>Net WPM = (Correct Keystrokes / 5) / Minutes</div>
          <div>Accuracy % = (Correct / Total Keystrokes) × 100</div>
          <div>CPM = Correct Characters Typed / Minutes</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Preeti Rules Cheat Sheet -->
    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        Essential Preeti Typing Rules & Ligatures Cheat Sheet
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-4">
        Preeti requires typing certain diacritics and ligatures in non-intuitive sequences. Here are the most critical rules to remember:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">1. Raswa Ikaar (ि)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Type <code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">l</code> BEFORE the consonant.<br>Example: <code class="font-mono">ls</code> = कि, <code class="font-mono">ld</code> = मि</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">2. Reph (र्)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Type <code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">{</code> (Shift + [) AFTER the letter.<br>Example: <code class="font-mono">s{</code> = र्क, <code class="font-mono">w{</code> = र्ध</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">3. Purna Viram (।)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Type period <code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">.</code> key.<br>Example: <code class="font-mono">.</code> = । (full stop in Nepali)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">4. Tra (त्र) & Tta (त्त)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]"><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">q</code> = त्र (tra)<br><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">Q</code> (Shift + q) = त्त (tta)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">5. Gya (ज्ञ) & Dda (द्द)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]"><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">1</code> = ज्ञ (gya)<br><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">2</code> = द्द (dda)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <span class="font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] block mb-1">6. Ksha (क्ष)</span>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]"><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">If</code> (Shift + i, then f) = क्ष<br><code class="font-mono text-[var(--accent-primary)]">I</code> alone produces half-ksha (क्ष्)</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: Speed Training Advice -->
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        Proven Strategies to Reach 40+ WPM in Nepali Typing
      </h3>
      <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside text-xs">
        <li><strong>Maintain Home Row Posture:</strong> Anchor your left hand on A-S-D-F (ब-क-म-ा in Traditional) and right hand on J-K-L-; (व-प-ि-स). Never hunt and peck with single fingers.</li>
        <li><strong>Focus on Rhythm Over Sprinting:</strong> High consistency (above 90%) yields fewer backspaces. Correcting a single mistake takes the time of typing three characters.</li>
        <li><strong>Practice Hard Conjuncts Daily:</strong> Familiarize yourself with complex ligatures such as राष्ट्रिय, अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय, दृष्टिकोण, and संविधान which frequently appear in government examinations.</li>
        <li><strong>Take Timed 5-Minute Tests:</strong> Use our 300-second Loksewa exam mode at least twice a day to build mental endurance for official test conditions.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
